# smoke.list — the curated ADRT_SMOKE=1 scenario set.
#
# One configuration only: a single 1280x800 screen with dynamic workspaces
# (GNOME defaults), which is what scripts/agent-test.sh starts by default.
# The list is an ordered subset of the existing tests/agent/A*.sh scenarios,
# chosen for speed and independence, at least one per feature area (a couple of
# areas get two or three) so a developer gets a fast "is this build sane"
# signal. The full suite (the A[0-9][0-9]* glob)
# stays the release gate; this only replaces the scenario *set*, never an
# assertion.
#
# Format: one scenario id per line, with or without a trailing `.sh`; blank
# lines and `#` comments are ignored. An entry whose file does not exist is a
# hard failure of the smoke run, named on stderr — the list can never silently
# drop a scenario when one is renamed.
#
# Feature -> scenario map (see docs/V2_MODEL.md sections and tests/MANIFEST.md):
#
#   tiling / split / axis            A01-pair-tiling, A64-vertical-workspaces
#   arrival routing (third window    A02-third-window
#     gets its own workspace)
#   focus (cycle + direction)        A121-focus-cycle-order,
#                                    A57-keyboard-focus-system
#   move (toward, onto a full        A127-swap-is-invertible,
#     workspace -> float)            A54-overview-move-onto-pair
#   resize ratio + undo              A09-undo
#   swap (invertible) + undo         A127-swap-is-invertible (invertible),
#                                    A101-undo-restores-instance-and-config
#                                    (undo of a drag-swap / un-float)
#   maximize / unmaximize ladders    A04-maximized-window,
#                                    A90-unmaximise-joins-pair-forming-left,
#                                    A91-unmaximise-parks-when-no-neighbour-
#                                    can-pair
#   fullscreen                       A57-keyboard-focus-system (behaviour),
#                                    A131-fullscreen-hides-highlight
#   float / above-floats             A11-float-toggle, A61-above-floats
#   minimize / reap                  A35-minimize-removes-workspace
#   lone-window maximize             A58-lone-window-maximized
#   workspaces (create / reorder /   A96-reorder-is-honoured-and-an-empty-
#     move / sticky)                 workspace-is-pruned, A117-arrival-side-rule,
#                                    A72-sticky-window-untiled
#   overview (coherence +            A56-coherence-sweep,
#     drop-is-a-move)                A74-overview-drop-is-a-move
#   registry / identity              A98-registry-lists-every-app
#   displays (plan / rescue / replay A112-workarea-change-replans-one-monitor
#     — rescues and replays are the (the one-monitor replan; rescue/replay
#     two-screen scenarios)          need two screens, so they stay in the suite)
#   session modes (pause/lock hide   A13-lock-screen
#     the border)
#   highlight (occlusion, fullscreen) A130-occlusion-hides-highlight,
#                                    A131-fullscreen-hides-highlight
#   undo (swap, un-float)            A101-undo-restores-instance-and-config
#   flags / trace / DumpState shape  A103-record-trace-shape
#
# Out of scope for a one-configuration smoke (kept in the full suite):
#   multi-monitor routing/drags/rescue/replay (A105-A111, A122, A124),
#   the four-monitor matrix (A81), the opt-in long churn run (A125).
# A cursor-follows-focus scenario would be added here only once the
# v2/cursor-centre branch lands and the capability probe reports it.
#
# --- tiling / split / axis ---
A01-pair-tiling
A64-vertical-workspaces
# --- arrival routing ---
A02-third-window
# --- focus ---
A121-focus-cycle-order
A57-keyboard-focus-system
# --- move ---
A127-swap-is-invertible
A54-overview-move-onto-pair
# --- resize + undo ---
A09-undo
